@startuml egress-decision
' UML activity diagram: the grant at start, then one CONNECT decision.
' Source of record for egress-decision.svg - render with the pinned PlantUML image.
title The egress decision: grant, then CONNECT

start
:read profile network.egress and the class allowlist;
if (profile destination outside the class?) then (yes)
  :refuse before start: the class is a ceiling;
  stop
endif
:grant = profile egress matched by class;
if (grant empty?) then (yes)
  :announce "this jail has no route out";
endif
:CONNECT host:port;
if (IP literal?) then (yes)
  :deny reason=ip-literal;
  stop
endif
if (in grant?) then (no)
  :deny not-in-profile or not-in-class;
  stop
endif
:resolve once, check every answer;
if (an answer is blocked?) then (yes)
  :deny blocked-<range>, no address tried;
  stop
endif
:connect pinned, audit allow;
stop
legend right
  DNS half: a granted name answers 127.0.0.1; any other name is nxdomain with
  reason=not-in-profile (the class has it, this jail was not granted it) or
  reason=not-in-class (the class does not have it either).
endlegend
@enduml
